        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/DSC03182Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p> </p>
<h3>Vision:<figure class="post__image post__image--left"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026.jpg" alt="" width="3465" height="2624" sizes="(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px" srcset="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-xs.jpg 640w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-sm.jpg 768w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-md.jpg 1024w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-lg.jpg 1366w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-xl.jpg 1600w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03160Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-2xl.jpg 1920w"></figure></h3>
<p>The idea of ​​bringing a piece of nature into the home is both fascinating and relaxing. I believe that this contact with less processed materials in our homes provides a link between the world of cement and plastic we live in and the nature that is our root on this planet. While the functionality of a table is important, leaving small indentations that recall the irregularity of nature is a subtle balance in the construction and design of our tables.</p>
<h3>Materials:</h3>
<div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="3" data-is-empty="false">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/gallery/DSC03181Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026.jpg" data-size="3936x2624"><img loading="lazy" src="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/gallery/DSC03181Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-thumbnail.jpg" alt="" width="720" height="480"></a></figure>
</div></div>
<p>Kiln-dried olive wood table, with small decorations and epoxy resin inlays.<br>Ideal for indoors, designed for apartments, with ample storage space underneath.<br>Minimalist and sturdy metal base.</p>
<p>Mostly handcrafted using traditional tools.<br>The quality of the materials used is very important to us, which is why we source premium woods and use high-quality finishing products. In this case, we rely on Rubiomonocoat's certification as a product that is both environmentally friendly and safe for people. as well for the glue used in some of the sections.</p>
<h3>Dimensions</h3>
<p>Size: 78cm long x 43cm wide x 46cm high</p>
<figure class="post__image"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026.jpg" alt="" width="3725" height="2518" sizes="(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px" srcset="https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-xs.jpg 640w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-sm.jpg 768w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-md.jpg 1024w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-lg.jpg 1366w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-xl.jpg 1600w ,https://woodworkbober.com./media/posts/1/responsive/DSC03175Table-Olive-and-epoxy-2026-2xl.jpg 1920w"></figure>
